86	    /**
87	     * Re-throws {@link AccessDeniedException} so Spring Security's {@code ExceptionTranslationFilter}
88	     * translates it as it normally would - 403 for an authenticated user lacking the required role,
89	     * or the configured entry point for an anonymous one. Without this, {@link #handleGeneralException}
90	     * would catch it and report an authorization failure as a 500.
91	     *
